# Development and test dependencies.
#
# requirements.in is included rather than repeated. It used to be a separate
# list with its own copy of the runtime dependencies, which meant CI installed
# only this file and quietly lost anything that was added to requirements.in
# without also being added here -- cryptography being the dependency that
# mattered, since PQXDH moved it into the runtime set.
#
# cryptography is listed explicitly as well. It arrives through requirements.in,
# but pinning the test-side use explicitly is what stops a test that
# cross-validates against an independent implementation from quietly depending
# on a transitive edge.
#
# pytest-asyncio was dropped: the suite is entirely synchronous and nothing
# imports it.

# Runtime dependencies, which the tests also need.
-r requirements.in

